{
  "a_galaxy_workflow": "true",
  "format-version": "0.1",
  "name": "FASTQ_PREPROCESS_GATK",
  "annotation": "FASTQ_PREPROCESS_GATK: Complete preprocessing pipeline for GATK variant calling\n\nWorkflow Steps:\n1. Optional UMI consensus calling from UMI-tagged reads\n2. Quality control and trimming with fastp\n3. Optional contamination removal with BBSplit\n4. Read alignment to reference genome\n5. Optional UMI tag copying from read names\n6. BAM merging and indexing\n7. BAM to CRAM conversion\n8. Mark duplicates (choice of standard GATK, Spark, or Sentieon)\n9. Base quality score recalibration (BQSR) table generation\n10. Apply BQSR recalibration\n11. Final CRAM/BAM output for variant calling\n\nConditional Paths:\n- UMI processing: Only when umi_read_structure is specified\n- BBSplit: Only when tools contains 'bbsplit'\n- Mark Duplicates variants: Standard GATK (default), Spark (faster), or Sentieon (commercial)\n- BQSR: Can be skipped with skip_tools parameter\n- Output format: CRAM (default) or BAM (when save_output_as_bam is true)\n\nRestart Points:\n- From alignment (CHANNEL_ALIGN_CREATE_CSV)\n- From mark duplicates (CHANNEL_MARKDUPLICATES_CREATE_CSV)\n- From base recalibration (CHANNEL_BASERECALIBRATOR_CREATE_CSV)\n- From recalibration (CHANNEL_APPLYBQSR_CREATE_CSV)",
  "steps": {
